          "secNumber": "8.16",
          "heading": "Unit 8 Review and Methodological Synthesis",
          "content": "Unit 8 synthesized sequential simulation, state space tracking, and modern simulation-based inference. We formulated state-space hidden Markov models and derived the Bayesian recursive filtering equations. We detailed Sequential Importance Sampling (SIS) and demonstrated how weight degeneration inevitably collapses particle diversity. We explored Sequential Importance Resampling (SIR) under multinomial, stratified, residual, and systematic resampling schemes, evaluating the Effective Sample Size $N_{\\text{eff}} = 1 / \\sum (w_t^{(i)})^2$. We examined Pitt and Shephard's Auxiliary Particle Filter (APF), showing how predictive lookahead auxiliary weights prevent particle starvation during informative observation updates. We analyzed Approximate Bayesian Computation (ABC) rejection and ABC-SMC algorithms for likelihood-free scientific models, and surveyed the Pseudo-Marginal theorem underpinning Particle MCMC (PMMH). Finally, we examined the Ensemble Kalman Filter (EnKF) for planetary-scale data assimilation and Neural Posterior Estimation (NPE) via normalizing flows.",
